<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:themes="clr-namespace:WpfLib.Themes"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <themes:SharedResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/brushes.xaml"/>
    </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>

    <!--
        The surface a popup sits on.

        Every pane had hand-rolled its own: a Border inside a Popup with
        AllowsTransparency off, no corner radius, no gap under the trigger, and
        a Background bound to an ancestor UserControl. Seven of them, all
        slightly different from each other and none matching the combo box
        drop-down, which is the one users see most.

        Wrap a popup's content in this instead:

            <Popup AllowsTransparency="True" VerticalOffset="4" ...>
                <Border Style="{StaticResource PopupSurface}" MinWidth="...">

        AllowsTransparency matters as much as the style does. With it off,
        every pixel the Border does not cover paints as the popup's own opaque
        surface, so rounded corners come out with hard black wedges in them.

        The background follows the host rather than being stated, because a
        drop-down is a continuation of the pane's own content. That is the
        opposite of ToolTip and ContextMenu, which are floating surfaces and
        commit to the dark PopupBrush in Brushes.xaml.

        PriorityBinding rather than a single ancestor: a task pane has a
        UserControl to bind to and a plain Window, like the demo hosts, does
        not. Bound to only the UserControl this produced null in the demos,
        and a null brush on an opaque popup paints black.

        NOT usable from inside a ControlTemplate. A StaticResource there throws
        when the template is instantiated in another HwndSource, which is
        exactly what a Popup is. Templates inline these values instead - see
        ComboBoxStyles and AddressBarStyles.
    -->

    <Style x:Key="PopupSurface" TargetType="Border">
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush"     Value="{StaticResource BorderBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius"    Value="4"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding"         Value="0,3"/>
        <Setter Property="Background">
            <Setter.Value>
                <PriorityBinding>
                    <Binding Path="Background" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}"/>
                    <Binding Path="Background" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource AncestorType=Window}"/>
                </PriorityBinding>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
        <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground">
            <Setter.Value>
                <PriorityBinding>
                    <Binding Path="Foreground" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}"/>
                    <Binding Path="Foreground" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource AncestorType=Window}"/>
                </PriorityBinding>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

</ResourceDictionary>
